# Copy to .env.local and adjust. Both are optional — the defaults match the backend's own
# compose stack (life-tracker-backend/compose.yaml), so a checkout works with no configuration.

# Where the dev server proxies /v1 to. Read by vite.config.ts at startup.
#
# 8080 is not a guess: compose publishes the app service as "8080:8080", and in the
# dependencies-only mode (the default) `bootRun` binds the same port on the host. Both of the
# backend's documented modes put the API on localhost:8080.
# VITE_BACKEND_ORIGIN=http://localhost:8080

# Base URL the generated client prefixes to every request.
#
# LEAVE THIS UNSET IN DEVELOPMENT. Setting it to http://localhost:8080/v1 makes the browser call
# the API cross-origin, and the backend has no CORS configuration at all — no
# CorsConfigurationSource, nothing in SecurityConfig — so every request would fail preflight.
# Unset, calls go to /v1 on the dev server's own origin and are proxied, which keeps them
# same-origin and needs nothing from the backend.
#
# Set it for a deployed build, where there is no dev server to proxy. Include the /v1, which is
# the application's own context-path (server.servlet.context-path in application.properties,
# ADR-0017) and not something a gateway adds:
#   VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.lifetracker.example/v1
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=
